course: dictionary
lesson: 13701
title: Insertion: putting something in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An insertion is the act of putting something into something else. It can also be the thing that is put in. The word comes from the verb insert, which means to put in. «The insertion of the missing word made the sentence clear.» The word was put into the sentence, so the sentence now makes sense.
explain: Look at the word parts: in means into, and -ion turns the verb into a noun, a name for an action or a thing. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «The putting in of the missing word made the sentence clear.» It still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. «The newspaper ran a small insertion about the school fair.» Here the insertion is the advert, the thing put in the newspaper. If the sentence were about doing something, insertion would mean the act of putting something in.
fact: Insertion means the act of putting something into something else.
fact: An insertion can also be the thing that is put in, such as extra words added to a text or an advert in a newspaper.
fact: In English, an insertion mark, a caret (^), shows where to add a missing word.
fact: In computing, the insertion point is where the cursor is when you type.
fact: In medicine, doctors carefully make an insertion when they put in a tube or a needle.
exercise: «The insertion of the missing word made the sentence clear.» What does insertion mean here? | The act of taking a word out | *The act of putting a word in | A word written in capital letters | A loud noise in the room
exercise: «The editor drew a small caret (^) under the gap.» What does the caret show? | *Where to add a missing word | Where the story ends | Which word is the longest | The name of the author
exercise: «The newspaper ran a small insertion about the school fair.» What is the insertion here? | The front page of the newspaper | A mistake that was taken out | *An advert put into the newspaper | The reporter who wrote the news
test: Which word means the act of putting something into something else? | Deletion | Election | *Insertion | Direction
test: «The doctor's careful insertion of the tube helped the patient breathe.» What does insertion mean here? | Cleaning the tube | Buying a new tube | *Putting the tube in carefully | Taking the tube out
exam: «The cursor shows the insertion point where your typing will appear.» What is the insertion point? | *Where the cursor is when you type | A picture you copy and paste | The place where the screen is switched off | The name of the computer
